            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>A crystal-pulse construct is a volatile and unpredictable creature, formed when an electrical field holds magically charged crystals in suspension. Existing in a constant state of flux, the construct must vent magical and electrical energy almost constantly to stabilize its form.</p>\n<p>While crystal-pulse constructs sometimes form spontaneously when lightning strikes a magical environment or other powerful currents encounter magically charged minerals, only deliberately calibrated constructs have the necessary equilibrium to remain animated for long. These stabler constructs are most commonly found guarding the laboratories of wizards and elementalists or wandering the Plane of Metal.</p>",
            "publication": {
